export declare const LIBRARY_INDEX_OVERVIEW = "# Shader-Craft Library Index\n\nUpstream generates this index from its GLSL library. Call these functions by name in an effect's programs, then run\n`bundleShader` to inline exactly what each program uses. Find candidates by searching the `shader-craft-library-*`\nreferences. Signatures are the upstream GLSL ones, with Noisemaker parameter names (`pixel` for the fragment's pixel\ncoordinate). The shader-craft library provides each function in GLSL and WGSL; where its own index differs from this\none, the library is authoritative. Library code reads no uniforms, only its parameters, and GLSL programs that use it\ndeclare `precision highp float;` and `precision highp int;`.\n\nWGSL has no overloading. A name with one GLSL signature keeps that name in WGSL; each signature of an overloaded name\nadds an underscore and one code per parameter: f, i, u for float, int, uint, f2-f4 for vec2-vec4, u2-u4 for uvec2-uvec4,\nm2-m3 for mat2-mat3. So `fbm(vec2 p, int octaves)` is `fbm_f2i` in WGSL, `sdBox(vec3, vec3)` is `sdBox_f3f3` and\n`saturate(float)` is `saturate_f`. GLSL out and inout parameters are `ptr<function, T>` parameters in WGSL.\n\nTags: **exact** is a true Euclidean distance, safe for blending, AO, shadows and offsets.\n**bound** never overestimates, so it is safe to march, but less accurate for offsets.\n**approx** has an exact surface but may overestimate in places; read its note for a safe step scale.\n\n## Contents\n\n- common - constants, rotation, remapping and shaping functions\n- hash - integer hashes and float wrappers for lattice ids\n- noise - value, gradient and simplex noise (2D/3D, analytic derivatives), fBm, turbulence and billow, domain warping, curl flow, Voronoi, dithering\n- pattern - tilings and antialiased procedural patterns\n- sdf3d - 3D signed distance primitives\n- sdf2d - 2D signed distance primitives for posters, icons, UI, motion graphics, and as profiles for opExtrude / opRevolve\n- operators - combine distances (booleans, smooth blends, chamfers, stairs) and reshape them (round, onion, extrude, revolve, elongate)\n- domain - transform the point BEFORE evaluating a distance (repetition, mirroring, polar sectors, folds, twist, bend)\n- architecture - stable building parameters and filtered facade fields\n- raymarch - sphere tracing, normals, soft shadows and ambient occlusion for SDF scenes\n- intersect - analytic ray-primitive intersections\n- camera - look-at frames, primary rays, field of view, thin-lens depth of field\n- shading - BRDF terms and practical lighting models\n- water - finite-depth wave dispersion, analytic wave derivatives, exact dielectric Fresnel and RGB attenuation\n- color - transfer functions, perceptual color (Oklab / OkLCh), palettes, luminance, blackbody light colors\n- tonemap - map scene-linear HDR to display range\n- volume - participating media (fog, smoke, clouds, haze)\n- atmosphere - skies and sun\n- post - antialiasing helpers, supersampling offsets, lens effects, grain and dithering, all usable inside one pass\n- debug - visualize intermediate fields\n";
